Distinguish between blocking and non-blocking assignments in Verilog. Draw the circuits for the following codes.

```verilog
module example5_5 (x1, x2, x3, Clk, f, g, h);
input x1, x2, x3, Clk;
output reg f, g;
always @(posedge Clk)
begin
f = x1 ~& x2;
g = f ~| x3;
h = g | f
end
endmodule
```

```verilog
module example5_5 (x1, x2, x3, Clk, f, g, h);
input x1, x2, x3, Clk;
output reg f, g;
always @(posedge Clk)
begin
f <= x1 ~& x2;
g <= f ~| x3;
h <= g | f
end
endmodule
```
